# Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile would bundle the local .git history (bloats
# the image), a developer's local node_modules (built for the host's OS/arch, which could
# silently overwrite the correctly-built Linux binaries from `npm install` inside the
# container), and -- worst case -- a local .env file with real secrets baked directly into
# an image layer if one happens to exist next to the Dockerfile.
.git
node_modules
downloads
data
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
